zygote_next: skip capabilities the kernel doesn't know

Android 17's native zygote (zygote_next) drops every capability outside
the requested bounding set, and first asks the kernel with
PR_CAPBSET_READ whether each one is in the set. It walks all
capabilities libcap knows, up to CAP_CHECKPOINT_RESTORE (40). Kernels
before 5.8 stop at CAP_AUDIT_READ (37) and answer EINVAL for 38-40,
and the .expect() turns that into a panic, so every child aborts.

On doha (4.14) this kills every app zygote started through
NativeZygoteProcess, which is how Chrome, Edge and other Chromium
browsers start their renderers on Android 17: the browser UI runs but
no page ever loads (doha_android#71).

A capability the kernel doesn't know can't be in the bounding set, so
treat EINVAL as "not in the set" and move on. Any other error still
panics as before.
---
 zygote/src/child_process.rs | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/zygote/src/child_process.rs b/zygote/src/child_process.rs
index f6ec741..122faba 100644
--- a/zygote/src/child_process.rs
+++ b/zygote/src/child_process.rs
@@ -83,7 +83,19 @@ pub(crate) fn re_initialize(
     if let Some(cap_bound) = spawn_params.cap_bound {
         for flag in cap_bound.complement().iter() {
             let cap = Capability::try_from(flag.bits().trailing_zeros()).unwrap();
-            if cap::cap_within_bound(cap).expect("Failed to check capability bound") {
+            // A kernel older than the capability (CAP_PERFMON, CAP_BPF and
+            // CAP_CHECKPOINT_RESTORE need 5.8/5.9) rejects PR_CAPBSET_READ
+            // with EINVAL. Such a capability can't be in the bounding set,
+            // so there's nothing to drop.
+            let within_bound = match cap::cap_within_bound(cap) {
+                Err(cap::CapabilityError::GetCapBoundFailure(errno))
+                    if errno as i32 == libc::EINVAL =>
+                {
+                    false
+                }
+                result => result.expect("Failed to check capability bound"),
+            };
+            if within_bound {
                 cap::cap_drop_bound(cap).expect("Failed to drop capability bound");
             }
         }
